0,"Design a software application that models a file system's hierarchical directory layout. The tool must enable users to execute fundamental tasks such as establishing, eliminating, and listing directories and files. Incorporate functionalities for appending a new file or folder beneath an existing entity, removing it, and showcasing the current directory's contents along with their sizes in bytes. Guarantee that the program maintains an accurate record of the cumulative size of all files and directories at each level of the structure. Furthermore, ensure that it alerts users when they attempt to create a file or folder with an already existing name in the same location, offering suitable error notifications.",680,,"['```python
class Directory:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self.name = name
        self.children = []
        self.total_size = 0

    def add_child(self, child):
        self.children.append(child)
        self.total_size += child.total_size if isinstance(child, Directory) else child.size

    def remove_child(self, child):
        if child in self.children:
            self.total_size -= child.total_size if isinstance(child, Directory) else child.size
            self.children.remove(child)

    def list_contents(self):
        for item in self.children:
            print(f""{item.name} - {item.__class__.__name__}: {item.total_size if isinstance(item, Directory) else item.size}"")

    def create_file(self, name, size=0):
        if any(file.name == name for file in self.children):
            raise ValueError(""File already exists."")
        self.children.append(File(name, size))

    def create_directory(self, name):
        if any(dir.name == name for dir in self.children):
            raise ValueError(""Directory already exists."")
        self.children.append(Directory(name))
        self.children[-1].parent = self

class File:
    def __init__(self, name, size=0):
        self.name = name
        self.size = size

root = Directory(""Root"")
```

This code provides a basic structure for representing a file system directory hierarchy using Python classes `Directory` and `File`. The `Directory` class can add, remove, and list its children as well as track the cumulative size of all its contents. The `File` class represents individual files with their names and sizes.

To create new directories or files within an existing directory, you can call the `create_directory` and `create_file` methods on a specific Directory instance, respectively. This code does not yet include error handling for creating items outside the root directory or recursively navigating through the directory structure, but it should serve as a starting point.']",0,[0],[],True,0,0,0,

